	)
	(gr_text "BOTTOM PASTEMASK"
		(at 186.69 94.996 0)
		(layer "B.Paste")
		(uuid "3de36807-00da-4572-8c3e-acd7ae04ca28")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom mirror)
		)
	)
	(gr_text " 1. When possible, reference designators were placed within components.\n 2. 3 tables are included on the assembly drawing as follows:\n   A. The component population that will set a color of D1 to either blink or stay solidly lit.\n   B. The component population that will change the blink rate of a color of D1 when that color is set to blink.\n   C. The component population that will set the power input configuration.\n 3. The PCB is design so that a color of D1 cannot be set to both blink and stay solidly lit.\n   A. Components for each configuration overlap on the Assembly due to this.\n 4. The PCB is design so that a power input with only batteries cannot be populated when the USB power input is enabled.\n   A. Components for each configuration overlap on the Assembly due to this.\n 5. When space is permitting, the component reference designator is inside the component outline.\n 6. The cathodes of D2, D3 and D4 are labeled with a 'K' on the Assembly Drawing and on the PCB Silkscreen.\n 7. The design was tested with an Inolux HV-5RGB60 Multi-Color LED.  This LED was selected due to the lower forward voltage.\n   A. A different LED can be used with the design if the LED has a common cathode on pin 2.  Tests with prior LEDs however had\n      issues properly blinking due to the higher forward voltage on the blue and green pins.\n   B. When powering the board with only coin cells (no USB input), the blinking does work due to a higher Vcc.  The USB input\n      requires a rectifying circuit and a subsequent drop down voltage regulator to keep consistent behavior between the coin\n      cells and USB power input.\n 8. Notes for each LED color are provided on the bottom silk screen to assist with assembly.\n   A. for the Inolux HV-5RGB60 Multi-Color LED the colors are as follows:\n     I. LED-1 is Red\n     I. LED-2 is Green\n     I. LED-3 is Blue"
		(at 85.598 151.003 0)
		(layer "F.Fab")
		(uuid "6e32194d-2b07-4c2d-85ce-1588dd79ab04")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.15)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
	)
	(gr_text "ASSEMBLY NOTES"
		(at 87.63 94.996 0)
		(layer "F.Fab")
		(uuid "b126fe9b-5c74-42a8-800b-e79adb25659b")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
	)
	(gr_text "REV B"
		(at 187.452 86.995 0)
		(layer "User.1")
		(uuid "8d1b982d-2659-4896-b935-3b08401540f8")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom mirror)
		)
	)
	(gr_text " 1. Customer is to be contacted if one or more items listed below are in violation.\n 2. Design is a 2 layer board with a copper weight of 1 oz.\n 3. Board thickness is 1.6 mm\n 4. All trace widths are 6 mils or greater in the current design.\n 5. All trace clearances are 6 mils or greater in the current design.\n 6. PCB revision is on the bottom layer of copper as noted.  Revision text is mirrored on this drawing.\n 7. Place manufaturer marking within the box on the bottom side of the board as noted.\n 8. All Gerber files contain Layer Defintion outside of the board artwork.\n 9. All Gerber files contain a trace of the board outline.\n10. Adhere to RoHS compliant process and ensure Pb-free manufacturing.\n11. Fabrication and inspect to meet IPC Class 2 standards.\n12. All Dimensions are in inches unless explictly noted.\n13. Placement of mounting hole to board orign is noted.\n14. Design only contains plated through holes.  Drill file and a Drill drawing in pdf format is included.\n15. Hole Size is not to exceed +/-2.5 mils of the documented size.\n16. Hole Position is not to exceed +/-2.5 mils of the documented size.\n17. All components holes has a minimum anunular ring size of 6 mils.\n18. Via Plating thickness must meet or exceed 1 mil.\n19. Test inaccordance with the latest revision of IPC-TM-650 2.4.22.\n20. The allowable warp or twist must not surpass 1% according to IPC-TM-650 2.4.22."
		(at 86.868 146.939 0)
		(layer "User.1")
		(uuid "9d0b3e36-97fc-438d-ba68-4ea4b9035920")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.15)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
	)
